First of all, eat a floating eye corpse for esp.  You need to be wearing an
amulet of lifesaving, not esp.  If you have a strong pet, your pet will start
killing unicorns for you.  You can use a cursed unicorn horn to go blind.
Make sure you have an uncursed horn to remove the undesired other effects,
like confusion or other effects.

If you have a reasonable level of strength I would recommend against the
gauntlets of power.  They are very useful when you have a weak, low-level
character, but once you start finding royal jelly and tins of spinach and
potions of gain ability (which you should *always* bless before using them
up), strength is one of the easier intrinsics to build up.  Once you have
acheived 18/** strength, you will actually loose strength when wearing the
gauntlets.

I recommend gauntlets of dexterity, a helm of brilliance, speed boots, and a
cloak of displacement.  I think my favorite is the displacement cloak.  That
really makes an incredible difference in the number of hits that you take.

Depending on what are the weaknesses of your character, you would choose a
different piece of armor to wish for first.

I generally wish for a blessed luckstone.  Then I max out my luck.  Then I
wish for 3 blessed scrolls of charging.  Then, I use my last wish (usually
there are three wishes) to get a piece of armor.  Then I use a scroll of
recharging (which only gives you one more charge).  Then I wish for a second
piece of armor (I always wish for blessed +3).  Now I have a (0) wand.  Next
I wish until I squeeze that last wish out of the wand, turning the wand to
dust.  This can take over 100 attempts, so keep trying.  Don't waste your
other charging scrolls on it, it will only recharge once.  So, from your first
wand, you get a blessed luckstone, 3 pieces of armor, and 2 blessed scrolls of
charging.  Now that your luck is maxed out, all your wishes will be better
performers for you.  If you happen to find another WOW, you can recharge it
without wishing for more scrolls.

